PARAMETER TYPE
There are three types:
    - "m"    METRIC PARAMETERS.  These are simply numbers.
    - "b"    BOOLEAN PARAMETERS.  These are 0 or 1 representing TRUE or FALSE (or ON and OFF).
    - "c"    CATEGORICAL PARAMETERS.  These are values representing some type of class label.  Some guidance on labels:
                 "operator6keyboardlevelscalingleftcurve" etc.  These values are 0 = negative linear, 1 = negative exponential, 2 = positive exponential, 3 = positive linear
                 "operator6keyboardlevelscalingrightcurve" etc.  These values are 0 = negative linear, 1 = negative exponential, 2 = positive exponential, 3 = positive linear
                 "algorithm"   These values are the individual algorithm numbers, 0...31
                 "lfowave"   These values are 0 = Triangle, 1 = Sawtooth Down, 2 = Sawtooth Up (Ramp), 3 = Square, 4 = Sine, 5 = Sample and Hold

